## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Ensure that functions revert explicitly when critical conditions are not met, such as failure in external calls, insufficient gas, or invalid state changes.
Adopt safe transfer patterns, such as the Checks-Effects-Interactions pattern, to ensure that state changes are executed before any external calls are made.


